1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
Everybody plants a tree.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Nobody finds out what happened to it.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
A birthday.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A school drive.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
A company afternoon.

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
They plant it, they take the photo, they post it,

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
and that is where it ends.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The planting is an event.

9
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
The keeping alive is a year.

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,000
So how much of it lives?

11
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
India's national auditor spent ten years going and looking.

12
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Of a two point eight million hectare afforestation target,

13
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
about five percent was actually achieved.

14
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
At seventy percent of the sites they assessed,

15
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
there was little or no improvement in tree cover at all.

16
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
One site reported two thousand plantings.

17
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Thirty saplings were found on the ground.

18
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
None of them had survived.

19
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
And here is the part that explains the rest.

20
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Of five hundred and fifty six plantation records,

21
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
four hundred and thirty one did not say what was planted,

22
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
where it stood, or whether it lived.

23
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
There is no record of what survived,

24
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
because nobody was ever asked to keep one.

25
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Planting is not the solution.

26
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Keeping it alive is.

27
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
And we already pay people to do boring things.

28
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Pay a credit card bill on time, and you earn points.

29
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Order dinner, take a taxi, board a flight.

30
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Points.

31
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Water the tree you planted last year,

32
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
and nothing happens at all.

33
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Rooted pays you for keeping it alive.

34
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Register a plant once, then do the small jobs it needs,

35
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,000
photographed as you do them.

36
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Every one that checks out earns points.

37
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,000
It is a website.

38
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
There is nothing to install, and it works with no signal.

39
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,000
You do not have to know anything about the plant.

40
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Every plant carries its own coordinates,

41
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:51,000
and the schedule moves with the weather actually over it.

42
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Rain pushes the next watering out.

43
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Heat pulls it in.

44
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
So nobody has to babysit it.

45
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
It tells you the job, on the day the job is due.

46
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Water, on this species own interval,

47
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
moved by the rain and the heat.

48
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Feeding, with what this plant actually wants,

49
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,000
and a reminder to use less than you think,

50
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,000
because fertiliser the roots do not take ends up in the

51
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,000
groundwater.

52
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Pests,

53
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
with what actually goes wrong with this species and the mildest

54
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,000
thing that works,

55
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,000
because a spray kills the ladybirds that were handling it for

56
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:25,000
you.

57
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
And a weekly look while it is establishing,

58
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
which is when losing it is most likely and least visible.

59
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Every plant also carries a health score.

60
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
It is built from how the watering has gone against the schedule

61
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
this species wants, and how long the run is.

62
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Thriving, steady, watch it, at risk.

63
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
And one sentence saying what moved it.

64
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
What it does not do is read the leaves and tell you the plant is

65
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:52,000
sick.

66
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
A yellow leaf has a dozen causes,

67
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,000
and a number invented from one is a number that gets trusted.

68
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,000
When it is time,

69
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
the camera tells you what would make the shot pass.

70
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Out loud,

71
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,000
because whoever is doing this is holding a watering can.

72
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
It reads the frame twice a second, on the phone,

73
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
and nothing is uploaded to do it.

74
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Tilt down so the soil is in frame.

75
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Then the ring around the shutter turns green.

76
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Then the photograph is checked,

77
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
and every check says the number it measured.

78
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
That it came off the camera and not a file picker.

79
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
The time, taken on our side.

80
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,000
The location, against where this plant was registered.

81
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,000
And for watering,

82
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
soil at least five percent darker than that plant's own dry

83
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
baseline.

84
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
That threshold was measured, not guessed.

85
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
This is the one that matters.

86
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
If photographing any plant earned points,

87
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
the points would be worth nothing.

88
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:54,000
So OpenCV finds keypoints in this photograph and in the plant's

89
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
first one, matches them,

90
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
and asks whether they agree on a single viewpoint.

91
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
The same plant returns four hundred and eighty five.

92
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,000
A different plant of the same species, in a similar pot,

93
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,000
returns four.

94
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Registering a plant checks the photograph before it accepts it.

95
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Point it at a notebook and it says so.

96
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:20,000
A plain object scores nought point two percent as a plant.

97
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,000
The least convincing real plant still scored nine.

98
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Point it at a plant and it works out what that plant is.

99
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Seventy-eight species,

100
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
searched by the names people actually use.

101
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,000
And five profiles for anything not on the list,

102
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:38,000
because knowing a plant's name and knowing how to keep it alive

103
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,000
are different jobs.

104
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,000
The whole premise is that people forget.

105
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
So this cannot wait to be opened.

106
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:50,000
When a task comes due, the same message goes out on WhatsApp,

107
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
on email, and as a text.

108
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,000
A name, a plant and a date go to the server.

109
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,000
No photographs.

110
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
No coordinates.

111
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Those never leave the phone.

112
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Organisations spend heavily on planting drives every year,

113
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
and get back a photograph from planting day.

114
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Rooted produces the record of what actually survived,

115
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
and every point in it traces to one verified task.

116
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
That record is what funds the rewards.

117
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
The offers in the app are stand-ins,

118
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:23,000
because naming a real company in a demo would put words in their

119
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
mouth.

120
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Two things did not survive contact with a measurement.

121
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
I tried to work out the species on the device,

122
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
from colour and texture.

123
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
It got the right answer first zero times out of seventeen.

124
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
And the check that says this is the same plant used to compare

125
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,000
brightness grids.

126
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,000
A photograph of a different neem tree walked straight through

127
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:45,000
it.

128
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Against eight percent for guessing at random.

129
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:52,000
It was the weakest thing in the app wearing the name of the

130
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:52,000
strongest.

131
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:55,000
So it was measured, thrown away, and replaced.

132
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
We reward people for spending money.

133
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Rooted rewards them for keeping something alive.

134
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Plant it.

135
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Keep it.

136
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Get paid for it.

137
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Nothing in here reports a number it did not measure.